# Godot 4.7 Rules

This is a **Godot 4.7** project. Default to Godot 4.7 APIs and reject Godot 3 patterns.

## Strict API rules

- Use `CharacterBody3D` / `CharacterBody2D` (NOT `KinematicBody*`)
- Use `Node3D` (NOT `Spatial`)
- Use `await signal.timeout` (NOT `yield(signal, "timeout")`)
- Use `signal.connect(callable)` Callable syntax (NOT `connect("name", self, "method")`)
- Use `@export`, `@onready`, `@tool` (NOT `export`, `onready`, `tool`)
- Use `move_and_slide()` with no argument (NOT `move_and_slide(velocity)`)
- Use `Time.get_ticks_msec()` (NOT `OS.get_ticks_msec()`)
- Use `randi_range()` / `randf_range()` (NOT `randi() % N` / `randf() * N`)
- Use `FileAccess.open()` (NOT `File.new()`)
- Use `create_tween()` + `tween_property()` (NOT `Tween.new()` + `interpolate_property`)
- Use `instantiate()` (NOT `instance()`)
- Use `process_frame` / `physics_frame` signals (NOT `idle_frame` / `idle_physics_frame`)

## Project conventions (giac-mo-co-tich)

- GDScript, PascalCase classes, snake_case functions/variables
- Signals prefixed with their domain (no generic `signal_changed`)
- Composition over inheritance — split complex nodes into `[parent]_[purpose].gd` components
- File ≤ 200 lines, functions ≤ 50 lines
- Vietnamese for game-logic comments, English for technical comments
- Per-tunable values via `@export`, never hardcoded
- Weather/profile state via `Resource` swap, never mutate `.tres` in-place
- Always verify changes in Godot editor (F5) before committing

## When asked to write code

1. Check the existing scene in `src/` for matching patterns first
2. Read one nearby correct file before generating — match its API style
3. Use `@export var` for anything tunable; `@onready var x: Type = $Child` for node refs
4. Static-type parameters and returns
5. Use `push_error()` / `push_warning()` for runtime guards, not silent fallbacks

## When NOT to apply this rule

- C# files (Godot supports C#, but this project is GDScript-only)
- Addon scripts under `addons/` that target their own engine version (e.g., phantom_camera 4.4 compat)
- Generated import files (`.gd.uid`, `.tscn.uid`, `.import`)

## Companion skills

- `godot-4.7-game-dev` — strict patterns reference
- `godot-gdscript-patterns` — general 4.x patterns
- `godot-mcp` — MCP server integration for live scene inspection